      <title>Guinea-Bissau denies it has approved controversial vaccine trial in newborns</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/14/guinea-bissau-vaccine-hepatitis-b-trial-denial</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Health minister says government ‘did not authorize’ Danish-led hepatitis B trial in babies backed by RFK Jr&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/guinea-bissau"&gt;Guinea-Bissau&lt;/a&gt; has not approved the controversial &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/society/hepatitis-b"&gt;hepatitis B&lt;/a&gt; study in newborns that would be funded by the US government and private partners, the African country’s minister of health said on Tuesday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The study, which would not investigate the safety or effectiveness of vaccines but would instead track “nonspecific” health outcomes like overall mortality or neurodevelopmental conditions, has been championed by Robert F Kennedy Jr, secretary of the US Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) and a longtime anti-vaccine activist.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/14/guinea-bissau-vaccine-hepatitis-b-trial-denial"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
