      <title>Joni Mitchell becomes US citizen: ‘A journey that began 62 years ago’</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/oct/14/joni-mitchell-becomes-us-citizen-a-journey-that-began-62-years-ago</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Canada-born singer-songwriter, 82, posts footage of citizenship ceremony to Instagram&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Joni Mitchell has become a US citizen, after first moving to the country in the mid-1960s. The Canada-born singer-songwriter, 82, posted footage of her citizenship ceremony on her Instagram account, along with a photo of her next to an American flag, accompanied by the caption: “A journey that began 62 years ago.”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It means that Mitchell can now vote in US elections, something that she had complained she wasn’t able to do.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/oct/14/joni-mitchell-becomes-us-citizen-a-journey-that-began-62-years-ago"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
