      <title>Intense waves and floods batter California waterfront homes and boardwalks</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/13/california-storm-floods</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Boardwalk destroyed in Long Beach and homes damaged, while Baja California in Mexico and Las Vegas also affected&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Southern &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"&gt;California&lt;/a&gt; coastal communities are picking up the pieces after a weekend of extreme weather brought flooding that overtook city streets and intense waves battered beachside homes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The remnants of Tropical Storm Rachel hit &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/mexico"&gt;Mexico&lt;/a&gt;’s Baja California over the weekend as well as southern California and Las Vegas. While meteorologists noted that Rachel weakened into a post-tropical cyclone as it approached California, it still left a trail of destruction.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/13/california-storm-floods"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
