      <title>How a scandal engulfing Brazil’s top court could return the Bolsonaros to power</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/scandal-brazil-court-jair-flavio-bolsonaro-power-election-moraes-lula</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The judge who helped convict Jair Bolsonaro is caught up in a crisis that could benefit his son and damage Lula&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/10/marina-silva-flavio-bolsonaro-the-amazon-brazil-president-far-right"&gt;Marina Silva on Flávio Bolsonaro: He will try to finish his father’s ‘perverse project’ to destroy the Amazon&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thundering to a crowd of thousands of far-right supporters in São Paulo on 7 September, Brazil’s Independence Day, the senator Flávio Bolsonaro focused less on his opponent in the &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/07/flavio-bolsonaro-advance-brazil-election-jolt-climate-campaigners"&gt;presidential election&lt;/a&gt;, the leftist president Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, than on someone who is not running at all.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;“Whoever votes for Lula is voting for &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/08/judge-alexandre-de-moraes-jair-bolsonaro-trial"&gt;Alexandre de Moraes&lt;/a&gt;,” Bolsonaro shouted, referring to the shaven-headed supreme court justice once &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/technology/article/2024/aug/31/x-offline-brazil-elon-musk"&gt;described as “Voldemort”&lt;/a&gt; by Elon Musk.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/scandal-brazil-court-jair-flavio-bolsonaro-power-election-moraes-lula"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
